{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The second time</b><br>He compared the pupil of the eye to doves that are beside streams of water, and they are the white of the eyes." "<b>The third time</b><br>\"His eyes.\" [i.e.] the ministers of His angels, as in the words of Zechariah, concerning one stone: \"seven eyes,\" and he said: \"these seven — the eyes of YHWH — they roam throughout all the earth.\""], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "Bracketed abbreviation [ז׳] resolved as '[כלומר]' (i.e.), by inference from parallel usage; the exact expansion is uncertain. The Zechariah citations blend Zechariah 3:9 and 4:10."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:31.572280973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}